[agent:result] # --- `mlpab run` must be FOREGROUND, never piped or backgrounded ---------------
[agent:result] # A nested `mlpab run` (spawned from inside another agent session) must stay
[agent:result] # synchronous. Two fatal ways a caller tries to "background" it:
[agent:result] #   - Piping (`mlpab run … | head`/`| tail`): downstream exits after N lines and
[agent:result] #     SIGPIPE-kills `mlpab run` mid-build, but the Bash tool returns 0 (head's
[agent:result] #     exit), so the caller reads truncated build output, thinks the run
[agent:result] #     started, and polls a dead run forever via `sleep`/`tail`.
[agent:result] #   - Backgrounding (trailing `&`): detaches the same way.
[agent:result] # Neither is caught by `run_in_background` (a tool flag, not shell syntax), so the
